I think one of the most touching things  about seeing the children at the funeral  was the little horseshoe Broach that  Charlotte was wearing on her coat and we  understand this was gifted her from the  queen it's just so perfect it was it was  small it was meaningful it signified the  Queen's love of horses and I'm sure  there will be other pieces that we'll  see over the years that the queen has  left for her great-granddaughter but it  was again that sense of continuity and  sentimental value attached to pieces of  jewelry like that that signal how close  the queen clearly was I think there was  a Sentimental side to the queen and I  think um you know she was very keen to  have those pieces that probably had  great meaning to her in the horse she  would have been you know it's a very  sweet gesture because of the Queen's  love of horses and she wanted those  pieces passed down and specifically that  piece to princess Charlotte I think you  know as the Prince of Wales said in his  statement he he felt hugely grateful  that his family got to spend so much  time with the queen I mean Kate had 20  years to really get to know the Monarch  what a privilege as a future Queen  consort hugely important as well but not  just that the queen had a lot of time  with her great grandchildren the queen  would Host this wonderful sleepover at  Balmoral in August and invite all of the  grandchildren and the great  grandchildren and she looked forward to  that weekend I think probably more than  any other it was always noisy when  Prince Philip was still alive he made  sure he wasn't around because there were  too many screaming children but the  queen absolutely loved it and I think  it was massively important to her that  she got to spend that time with her  family  [Music]  [Music]
 

